# Test: offline validate (query mode, S-3) and boot agree on an external plugin's YANG module
#
# Question: for a config under an external plugin's own root, does `ze config
# validate` with no ze listening query the declared external program in declare
# mode (`ZE_PLUGIN_MODE=declare`, never its run loop), join its YANG module,
# accept a valid section and refuse an out-of-range leaf, matching `ze start`
# which accepts and delivers the valid section?
# Why not a unit test: the verdicts come from two entries of the binary.
# Validate runs the plugin in query mode (S-3) and joins its Stage 1 schema
# offline; boot starts the plugin live, reads its module at Stage 1 and loads
# against the joined schema. Only running both proves both entries agree on the
# external plugin's module.
#
# Under S-3 (plan/release/fixes/spec-explicit-plugin-and-attach-config.md,
# AC-18), Thomas reversed the earlier ruling that offline validation starts no
# external program: offline commands that parse a config now query each declared
# external program in declare mode (never its run loop), validate against its
# declared YANG module, and print the queried plugins.
#
# The exit assertion is of the DAEMON'S own exit. `then=stop` on the await
# makes the runner wait for daemon.ready and for the awaited line, stop the
# daemon itself, and compare the code the daemon ended with
# (docs/architecture/testing/ci-format.md, "Await", step 3). So exit 0 means
# the daemon started, ran the plugin and stopped cleanly.
#
# ze.ssh.port points validate's ask at the runner's $PORT, where nothing
# listens during steps 1 and 2. The daemon of step 3 configures no SSH listener,
# so the option does not reach it.
#
# VALIDATES: S-3 / AC-18 of spec-explicit-plugin-and-attach-config.md beside
#   AC-1 and AC-2 of spec-plugin-external-yang-at-startup.
# PREVENTS: offline validate disagreeing with boot on an external plugin's YANG
#   module, accepting an out-of-range value, or starting the plugin's run loop.

option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT

tmpfs=ze.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bus {
	endpoint acme-monitor {
		external {
			run "le test fixture plugin/external-yang valid";
		}
		encoding json;
	}
}

acme-monitor {
	target probe-a
	interval 5
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=bad.conf:terminator=EOF_BAD
bus {
	endpoint acme-monitor {
		external {
			run "le test fixture plugin/external-yang valid";
		}
		encoding json;
	}
}

acme-monitor {
	target probe-a
	interval 11
}
EOF_BAD

# No ze running: validate queries acme-monitor in declare mode (S-3), joins its
# YANG module, accepts the valid section, and names the queried plugin without
# starting its run loop.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate ze.conf:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid: ze.conf
expect=stdout:contains=queried external plugins: acme-monitor
reject=stdout:contains=unknown top-level keyword
reject=stderr:contains=FIXTURE: external-yang

# Negative: the queried YANG module's range (1..10) is enforced offline.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate bad.conf:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=configuration invalid: bad.conf
expect=stdout:contains=queried external plugins: acme-monitor
expect=stdout:contains=interval
reject=stdout:contains=unknown top-level keyword

# Boot runs the plugin, joins its module and delivers the section.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze start ze.conf:timeout=30s
await=stderr:contains=FIXTURE: external-yang generation 1 ready:then=stop
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=FIXTURE: external-yang configure root=acme-monitor leaves=[acme-monitor/interval=5 acme-monitor/target=probe-a]
reject=stderr:contains=unknown top-level keyword
reject=stderr:pattern=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
